.TH CHKCONFIG 8 "August 4, 2026" "ReBSD" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
chkconfig \- examine or change system configuration flags
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chkconfig
[
.B \-s
]
.br
.B chkconfig
.I flag
.br
.B chkconfig
[
.B \-f
]
.I flag
[
.B on
|
.B off
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chkconfig
provides the IRIX-style interface to the system configuration flags kept in
.IR /var/config .
With no operands it lists every flag and its state, sorted by flag name.
The
.B \-s
option sorts the list by state and then by name.
.PP
With a single
.I flag
operand,
.B chkconfig
exits with status zero when the flag exists and is on, and status one when it
is off or does not exist.  No output is produced.
.PP
The optional
.B on
or
.B off
operand changes the flag.  The flag file must already exist unless
.B \-f
is specified.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/config
System configuration flag directory.  A flag is on when its file contains the
string
.BR on ;
all other contents mean off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For a query, zero means on and one means off or absent.  For listing or update
operations, zero means success and nonzero means an error occurred.
